<Base locale={locale} section="practical-info" title="Getting to Marienbad — Marienbad.com" description="How to reach Mariánské Lázně: flights, trains, buses, driving. Distances, travel times and practical tips.">
  <PillarPage locale={locale} title="Getting to Marienbad" description="Mariánské Lázně is located in western Bohemia, close to the German border — easily accessible from Munich, Prague and across Central Europe.">
    <h2>Location</h2>
    <p>Mariánské Lázně (Marienbad) lies in the <strong>western tip of the Czech Republic</strong>, in the Slavkov Forest (Kaiserwald), just 30 km from the Bavarian border. Its convenient location makes the town easily accessible from Germany, Austria and the wider region.</p>

    <h2>By Air</h2>
    <h3>Prague Airport (PRG) — 170 km</h3>
    <p>Prague Václav Havel International Airport is the main gateway. From Prague to Marienbad is approximately <strong>2 hours by car</strong> or <strong>3 hours by bus</strong>. Several shuttle services offer direct transfers to the spa hotels.</p>

    <h3>Karlovy Vary Airport (KLV) — 50 km</h3>
    <p>The small regional airport offers seasonal connections to selected European cities. Just 50 km away — approximately <strong>45 minutes</strong> by car.</p>

    <h3>Munich Airport (MUC) — 300 km</h3>
    <p>A practical option for travellers from southern Germany and international long-haul connections. Approximately <strong>3 hours</strong> by car via the A9/A93 motorways.</p>

    <h2>By Train</h2>
    <p><strong>Mariánské Lázně railway station</strong> has regular connections:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>From Prague:</strong> approximately 3 hours (changing in Plzeň/Pilsen). The route through the Slavkov Forest is one of the most scenic railway journeys in the Czech Republic.</li>
      <li><strong>From Plzeň:</strong> approximately 1.5 hours direct</li>
      <li><strong>From Karlovy Vary:</strong> approximately 1 hour</li>
      <li><strong>From Cheb:</strong> 25 minutes — with connections to international trains to/from Germany</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Via Cheb, there are connections to the German rail network (Nuremberg, Hof, Munich).</p>

    <h2>By Bus</h2>
    <p><strong>FlixBus</strong> and <strong>RegioJet</strong> connect Marienbad with:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Prague (approximately 2.5 hours)</li>
      <li>Plzeň, Karlovy Vary, Cheb</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Coaches offer WiFi, power outlets and refreshments. The bus station is a short walk from the town centre.</p>

    <h2>By Car</h2>
    <h3>From Prague (170 km, approx. 2 hours)</h3>
    <p>Take the D5 motorway towards Plzeň, then follow signs via R21 to Mariánské Lázně. Well signposted.</p>

    <h3>From Munich (300 km, approx. 3 hours)</h3>
    <p>A9 northbound, A93 to the border crossing at Pomezí nad Ohří/Schirnding, then continue to Mariánské Lázně.</p>

    <h3>From Nuremberg (200 km, approx. 2.5 hours)</h3>
    <p>A6/A93 to the border, then follow signs to Mariánské Lázně.</p>

    <h3>Tolls and Vignette</h3>
    <p>A <strong>motorway vignette</strong> is required for Czech motorways. You can purchase it electronically at <strong>edalnice.cz</strong> or at border crossings and petrol stations.</p>

    <h2>Distance Table</h2>

    | From | Distance | Drive Time |
    |------|----------|-----------|
    | Prague | 170 km | 2:00 h |
    | Munich | 300 km | 3:00 h |
    | Nuremberg | 200 km | 2:30 h |
    | Karlovy Vary | 48 km | 0:45 h |
    | Plzeň | 80 km | 1:15 h |
    | Dresden | 250 km | 3:00 h |
    | Vienna | 380 km | 4:00 h |

    <h2>Transfer Services</h2>
    <p>All <strong>Ensana Spa Hotels</strong> can arrange airport transfers. Many guests book a private transfer directly from Prague or Munich Airport — comfortable and stress-free after a long journey.</p>

    <p>The hotel reception can also arrange <strong>local taxis</strong> and <strong>car hire</strong> for excursions in the region.</p>
  </PillarPage>
</Base>
